{"name":"Cream of Mushroom","hex":"#ebd1be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"},{"term":"mushroom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the fleshy fruiting bodies of fungi typically produced above ground on soil or on their food sources (such as decaying wood).","A fungus producing such fruiting bodies."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having characteristics like those of a mushroom, for example in shape or appearance, speed of growth, or texture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mushroom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cream of mushroom soup","blocks":[{"text":"Cream of mushroom soup is a simple type of soup where a basic roux is thinned with cream or milk and then mushrooms or mushroom broth are added."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Cream_mushroom_soup_3.jpg/330px-Cream_mushroom_soup_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_of_mushroom_soup"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Mushroom","blocks":[{"text":"A mushroom is the fleshy, spore-bearing fruiting body of a fungus, typically produced above ground on soil or another food source. A toadstool generally refers to a poisonous mushroom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jpg/330px-Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mushroom"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2019-02-08_00_14_59_A_can_of_Campbell%27s_Condensed_Cream_of_Mushroom_Soup_in_the_Franklin_Farm_section_of_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2019-02-08_00_14_59_A_can_of_Campbell%27s_Condensed_Cream_of_Mushroom_Soup_in_the_Franklin_Farm_section_of_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2019-02-08_00_14_59_A_can_of_Campbell%27s_Condens